There are a number of people who are motivated to code 
roguelike games from scratch.  I'm one of them.  But, in 
general, those who are motivated to code roguelike games 
from scratch are not motivated to exactly copy existing 
games.  

Even if I were to code "Neohack", in which everything in 
nethack were to be preserved unless I thought there was 
a good reason not to, there'd still be a bunch of major 
differences from nethack. 

I'd like people's opinions and reactions to this laundry 
list of game design choices.

* First and biggest?  For personal and moral reasons, I'd 
  refuse to put in items, monsters, and artifacts that are 
  subject to existing copyrights without express permission 
  from the copyright holders.  That eliminates Stormbringer, 
  Greyswandir, Sting, Orcrist .... and many others.  I'd 
  feel compelled to replace them with other items, but 
  the other items would be *DIFFERENT*.

* Magic markers probably wouldn't exist. They are almost
  always detrimental to the game.  If they did exist, they'd 
  be more class restricted to mages and priests than they 
  are now and more restricted in their use (especially in 
  spells not already known - the ability to write such 
  might vanish entirely or be limited to once per character 
  level). OTOH, scrolls and spellbooks would be more common 
  and more available in shops. 

* New puddings (and any other creature that reproduces 
  in dungeon realtime) would not be generated with new 
  equipment.  No very strong feelings about summoned 
  intelligent creatures, however. 

* Wands of wishing would always have 2-3 charges, but 
  would not recharge.  They'd be rarer.  Only one magic 
  lamp per game would give a wish.  Wishes for artifacts 
  would be likely to fail. 

* Artifact secondary powers (including resistances/
  immunities in most artifacts) would be slightly randomized.  
  Primary powers would be stable.  When you find a thing out 
  of legend, you may find that the legend, while accurate 
  in major points, has embellished a few details and gotten 
  others wrong.

* AC from prayer would be limited in the same way that 
  divine protection is limited now. In fact the limitation
  might apply to their sum.

* Unicorn Horns would be nerfed somehow.  There are 
  dozens of possible ways.

* Item curses cast by liches et al would mostly end when 
  that particular lich gets destroyed.  

* Blessing inventory would be increasingly unlikely to 
  work if you had more than 4 or 5 pieces of blessed 
  inventory already.  

* No poisoned item could ever be blessed.  No character 
  carrying poison or unholy water (or certain artifacts) 
  would be allowed to carry holy water at the same time. 

* No character carrying holy water (or certain other 
  artifacts) would be allowed to carry unholy water or 
  poison at the same time.

* I'd probably reduce the fooproofing subgame in other 
  ways too, and reduce the consequences of not bothering
  with it. I think it's boring.

* Artifact "Blasting" of cross-aligned wielders wouldn't 
  be on pickup only.  It would happen at random intervals 
  during play, maybe double or triple prayer timeout 
  intervals. Quest artifacts of particular classes might 
  sometimes blast wielders of other classes.

* #pray'ing while carrying a weapon or artifact whose 
  alignment is opposed to your God's, or which is holy 
  to some other God, might be a bit dangerous.  If 
  you're lucky, your God will thank you for your 
  "sacrifice" and take it from you.  If you're not so 
  lucky, or you've been *using* the item extensively, 
  then see the code for offended and angry Gods. 

